ine.core`: the original SIGSEGV core, moved out of the next\\n+  run's core output path to prevent overwrite.\\n+\\n+The source mirror beside this README is for reviewing the diagnostic edits.\\n+The executing code is in the container repository. No commit was made.\\n+\\n+## Interpretation\\n+\\n+A serialized success alone does not prove the pipeline is defective: it also\\n+changes queue timing, active batches, and the lifetime/interleaving of CUDA\\n+operations. A failure with the same stack would show that serialization alone\\n+does not eliminate the issue. Compare the actual capture and complete benchmark\\n+outcome before drawing either conclusion.\\n*** Update File: /home/ubuntu/tieredserve-crash-analysis.md\\n@@\\n-- Core: `/root/projects/tiered-serve/core`; process/LWP 13469\\n+- Core (preserved before the authorized serial diagnostic):\\n+  `/root/cd3-serial-diagnostic-backup/original-pipeline.core`; process/LWP 13469\\n+- Matching original native extension is preserved under\\n+  `/root/cd3-serial-diagnostic-backup/native/`.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:83136,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:45000,max_output_tokens:1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0e8fc-8b6b-7543-8632-90b988d576f4","create_time":1790615509.724202}}}
